{{!
    @template tool_vae/feasibility_page

    The page "Dossier de faisabilité", below its heading: what the page is for, the table of the sections and where each
    stands, the button to the deposits, and the way back to the dossier.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\feasibility_page. The template holds no logic.
    Every text and address is escaped (double braces), except two keys of HTML (triple braces): tablehtml, a table drawn by
    the template tool_vae/table (its texts and links are escaped by the template tool_vae/cell_content); buttonhtml, the
    button to the deposits made by the core ($output->single_button()).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - string, what the page is for
    * tablehtml - HTML: the table of the sections
    * buttonhtml - HTML: the button to the deposits
    * back - {url, label}: the way back to the dossier

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "This page helps you write your dossier de faisabilité, section by section.",
        "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable tool-vae-faisabilite\"><tbody><tr><td>Objectives</td></tr></tbody></table>",
        "buttonhtml": "<div class=\"singlebutton\"><button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\">Deposits</button></div>",
        "back": {"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/dossier.php?userid=7", "label": "Back to the dossier"}
    }
}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{{buttonhtml}}}
{{#back}}
<p><a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></p>
{{/back}}
